1
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:24,460
We sigh whenever we're about to come to a standstill

2
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:24,460
Owarinaki tabi no tochuu tachidomarisouna toki

3
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:30,710
While moving on this endless journey.

4
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:30,710
Fukai tameiki kobosu bokura wa

5
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:38,430
Everytime we lunge for it, it escapes and flies off.

6
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:38,430
Tsukamikaketewa mata hanareteitta

7
00:00:38,890 --> 00:00:45,850
But now, there's nothing to be afraid of

8
00:00:38,890 --> 00:00:45,850
Demo ima wa mou nanimo osoreru koto wa nai

9
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:53,780
The powerful ties that bind our hearts

10
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:53,780
Kokoro wo tsunagu tsuyoi kizuna wa

11
00:00:53,780 --> 00:00:59,240
Will never come loose.

12
00:00:53,780 --> 00:00:59,240
Keshite hodoke wa shinai sa

13
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:08,960
After a lifetime of searching, we finally arrived

14
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:08,960
Sagashitsuzukete tadoritsuita

15
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:14,760
Here, where the period lies.

16
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:14,760
Kono basho de piriodo ni

17
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:24,060
Let's change all our sorrow and rage to power.

18
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:24,060
Kanashimi ikari chikara ni kaete

19
00:01:24,060 --> 00:01:28,980
Destiny is right within our reach.

20
00:01:24,060 --> 00:01:28,980
Unmei wa sugu soba ni

21
00:01:33,020 --> 00:01:35,360
Along with the recovered Lan Fan,

22
00:01:35,360 --> 00:01:38,570
Ed engages in combat with the Homunculus Pride.

23
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:42,580
He works out a plan while his mettle is tested,

24
00:01:42,780 --> 00:01:46,450
and successfully retrieves Al.

25
00:01:47,330 --> 00:01:51,250
But Pride swallows Gluttony, a comrade of his,

26
00:01:51,250 --> 00:01:53,500
and obtains his abilities.

27
00:01:55,960 --> 00:01:59,880
Elsewhere, Mustang has reunited with Hawkeye and his men.

28
00:02:00,470 --> 00:02:04,970
They've kidnapped the Führer President's wife in order to hold her hostage.

29
00:02:06,040 --> 00:02:09,040
Filial Affection

30
00:02:06,040 --> 00:02:09,040
Filial Affection

31
00:02:10,810 --> 00:02:12,480
Wake up, Al.

32
00:02:13,230 --> 00:02:14,320
Hey, Al!

33
00:02:14,320 --> 00:02:15,570
Can you hear me?

34
00:02:15,570 --> 00:02:17,070
Alphonse!

35
00:02:19,110 --> 00:02:20,360
This scent...

36
00:02:22,070 --> 00:02:23,700
Edward Elric.

37
00:02:24,740 --> 00:02:29,500
I'm sure Hohenheim will have no choice but to show himself if I were to capture you.

38
00:02:50,520 --> 00:02:51,270
Ed!

39
00:03:05,660 --> 00:03:06,700
Young master!

40
00:03:06,700 --> 00:03:08,040
Sorry,

41
00:03:08,330 --> 00:03:09,660
it's Greed now.

42
00:03:10,710 --> 00:03:11,830
You scum...

43
00:03:11,830 --> 00:03:13,460
Give young master back his body!

44
00:03:13,460 --> 00:03:15,710
No can do.

45
00:03:16,790 --> 00:03:17,800
Here he comes!

46
00:03:25,850 --> 00:03:26,550
Are you okay?!

47
00:03:35,060 --> 00:03:36,690
I don't need your help!

48
00:03:36,690 --> 00:03:37,770
Shut up!

49
00:03:37,770 --> 00:03:40,280
Your arm hasn't even fully recovered yet, right?!

50
00:03:41,280 --> 00:03:42,490
So what?!

51
00:03:42,700 --> 00:03:45,740
Just worry about yourself for now.

52
00:03:45,740 --> 00:03:47,910
I'm going to need your help later, you know.

53
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,420
Keep going!

54
00:03:54,420 --> 00:03:56,670
Sorry, I couldn't finish him.

55
00:03:56,880 --> 00:03:58,880
Heh, don't worry about it.

56
00:03:59,130 --> 00:04:01,380
I can't blame you for not being able to beat him.

57
00:04:02,090 --> 00:04:04,630
Even from my perspective, he's a monster.

58
00:04:11,850 --> 00:04:12,770
Wake up!

59
00:04:13,810 --> 00:04:14,940
Alphonse!

60
00:04:18,940 --> 00:04:19,940
Huh?

61
00:04:19,940 --> 00:04:21,110
Dad?

62
00:04:21,610 --> 00:04:22,610
Yo.

63
00:04:26,490 --> 00:04:27,490
So...

64
00:04:27,490 --> 00:04:29,330
If you're here...

65
00:04:29,330 --> 00:04:30,740
Am I in Kanama?

66
00:04:30,740 --> 00:04:31,740
Yup.

67
00:04:32,370 --> 00:04:33,790
Why am I...

68
00:04:33,790 --> 00:04:35,210
Since when...

69
00:04:36,500 --> 00:04:38,000
I remember now! Pride!

70
00:04:38,580 --> 00:04:42,460
Dad, the Homunculus Pride is inside me!

71
00:04:42,460 --> 00:04:45,550
Yeah, I heard everything from Mr. Gorrilius.

72
00:04:45,550 --> 00:04:46,630
It's Darius.

73
00:04:47,050 --> 00:04:48,550
Drats...

74
00:04:48,550 --> 00:04:52,560
It felt so disgusting. It was as if he was interfering with my soul.

75
00:04:52,850 --> 00:04:57,900
They're like the alter ego of my alter ego.

76
00:04:58,690 --> 00:05:02,820
Since you're my son, it's probably easier for them to interfere with your soul through the blood seal.

77
00:05:06,150 --> 00:05:07,450
Old Man Fu!

78
00:05:11,490 --> 00:05:14,000
Please treat his injuries.

79
00:05:14,950 --> 00:05:16,500
How are things going over there?

80
00:05:16,910 --> 00:05:19,380
Are you Edward's father?

81
00:05:19,380 --> 00:05:20,420
Yeah.

82
00:05:23,340 --> 00:05:27,970
The shadowy monster devoured Gluttony, and we hardly stand a chance.

83
00:05:28,470 --> 00:05:32,810
Greed and Edward are fighting him, but things aren't looking too good.

84
00:05:35,060 --> 00:05:36,600
It's all my fault...

85
00:05:36,600 --> 00:05:40,020
Everyone's in danger because I was captured by Pride...

86
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:46,690
There's an unlimited source of light due to the fire, and I've already used up all of my flash bangs.

87
00:05:46,690 --> 00:05:48,570
We can't use that same trick again.

88
00:05:49,570 --> 00:05:51,200
This isn't good.

89
00:05:52,070 --> 00:05:55,620
At this rate, the people living in the slums will be dragged into it as well.

90
00:05:57,790 --> 00:05:58,410
Dad.

91
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:02,790
You're a skilled alchemist, right?

92
00:06:04,300 --> 00:06:05,250
Of course.

93
00:06:05,250 --> 00:06:06,800
You'd be amazed.

94
00:06:07,590 --> 00:06:10,800
There's something I'd like to ask of you, considering your skill.

95
00:06:15,600 --> 00:06:16,890
Well then...

96
00:06:17,640 --> 00:06:20,230
The view is pretty clear now.

97
00:06:26,480 --> 00:06:28,990
No use in taking cover.

98
00:06:28,990 --> 00:06:30,950
You can't escape from my nose.

99
00:06:31,570 --> 00:06:32,990
Dammit...!

100
00:06:32,990 --> 00:06:34,830
Hey, you alive?!

101
00:06:34,830 --> 00:06:36,540
More or less...

102
00:06:36,950 --> 00:06:40,330
Should you really be worrying about others right now, Greed?

103
00:06:40,330 --> 00:06:43,920
I wonder how much more you can take at this point.

104
00:06:44,920 --> 00:06:46,420
You monster.

105
00:06:46,840 --> 00:06:51,180
A rather rude way to address your sibling, don't you think?

106
00:06:51,880 --> 00:06:53,430
Mind if I eat you?

107
00:06:53,430 --> 00:06:57,180
Eat me and you'll have a stomachache, Big Bro.

108
00:07:02,350 --> 00:07:04,730
Oh? Finally decided to show yourself?

109
00:07:05,060 --> 00:07:06,610
Hohenheim.

110
00:07:07,230 --> 00:07:11,150
Heroes are supposed to show up late.

111
00:07:11,610 --> 00:07:12,820
Heroes?

112
00:07:12,820 --> 00:07:15,780
So you think you're able to defeat me?

113
00:07:16,990 --> 00:07:19,200
Nah, that's impossible.

114
00:07:19,200 --> 00:07:22,210
You're pretty scary, after all.

115
00:07:30,340 --> 00:07:32,090
What is he planning?

116
00:07:33,130 --> 00:07:34,890
Is he aiming for something?

117
00:07:51,240 --> 00:07:51,990
He's coming!

118
00:07:57,030 --> 00:08:00,450
Wow, what a disappointing strategy.

119
00:08:02,410 --> 00:08:04,290
You just don't know when to give up!

120
00:08:10,210 --> 00:08:11,210
Al!

121
00:08:17,220 --> 00:08:20,680
So he came back, just to be taken hostage again?

122
00:08:21,770 --> 00:08:24,190
Your son is quite the odd one.

123
00:08:27,150 --> 00:08:29,320
Don't you dare...

124
00:08:29,860 --> 00:08:31,480
...to make fun of my son.

125
00:08:51,090 --> 00:08:54,170
Hohenheim!!!

126
00:09:06,640 --> 00:09:07,980
Amazing...!

127
00:09:08,230 --> 00:09:10,520
He actually sealed him in.

128
00:09:19,820 --> 00:09:21,370
What's the big idea?!

129
00:09:21,370 --> 00:09:23,490
You got Al stuck in there too!

130
00:09:23,490 --> 00:09:25,700
What the hell were you thinking?!

131
00:09:25,700 --> 00:09:27,670
It wasn't my idea.

132
00:09:28,250 --> 00:09:30,170
It was Al's.

133
00:09:34,340 --> 00:09:35,800
It worked!

134
00:09:35,800 --> 00:09:38,050
You can't use your ability in here.

135
00:09:38,300 --> 00:09:40,390
Is that really a cause for celebration?

136
00:09:40,390 --> 00:09:42,430
You can't escape either.

137
00:09:42,890 --> 00:09:45,850
If you crack open an exit to leave even for an instant...

138
00:09:45,850 --> 00:09:47,310
...I'll use my shadow and-

139
00:09:47,310 --> 00:09:49,310
I don't have the slightest intention of getting out of here.

140
00:09:51,560 --> 00:09:54,280
Why don't we engage in a test of wills, Selim?

141
00:09:54,280 --> 00:09:57,150
No, Homunculus Pride.

142
00:09:57,530 --> 00:10:01,700
My body doesn't require oxygen, light, or even food.

143
00:10:02,200 --> 00:10:05,540
You're going to quietly sit here with me for the entire day,

144
00:10:05,540 --> 00:10:08,960
until the Promised Day comes to an end.

145
00:10:10,830 --> 00:10:13,710
Defeating Pride in his current state would be difficult.

146
00:10:14,170 --> 00:10:17,920
And if we were to let him run loose,
it would cause massive damage to the surroundings.

147
00:10:17,920 --> 00:10:22,720
That's why Al offered to use himself as a decoy to trap him without engaging in combat.

148
00:10:23,390 --> 00:10:26,930
With this, we've gained some time to work out a plan.

149
00:10:26,930 --> 00:10:29,060
But you guys didn't even discuss it with me-

150
00:10:29,060 --> 00:10:30,560
He said,

151
00:10:31,270 --> 00:10:33,860
"If I were to tell Brother, he'd definitely be against it."

152
00:10:36,860 --> 00:10:41,740
He did the best he could to think of a way that would keep everyone alive.

153
00:10:41,740 --> 00:10:43,030
Don't get mad at him.

154
00:10:45,870 --> 00:10:48,620
Okay, let's start with putting this fire out.

155
00:10:54,920 --> 00:10:55,670
Al!

156
00:10:56,460 --> 00:10:57,420
Brother!

157
00:11:00,380 --> 00:11:01,380
Al!

158
00:11:02,050 --> 00:11:05,010
Sorry for doing this just after we were reunited.

159
00:11:07,180 --> 00:11:10,810
But I had to, because I was the one who caused this mess.

160
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:15,270
And besides, I only have to be in here for a day.

161
00:11:15,270 --> 00:11:17,610
I'll be fine, Brother.

162
00:11:23,030 --> 00:11:26,780
Lust is gone, Envy is gone, and Gluttony now, too.

163
00:11:27,620 --> 00:11:29,540
Wrath is at the the joint exercise in the east,

164
00:11:29,540 --> 00:11:31,460
and Pride can't move right now.

165
00:11:35,170 --> 00:11:39,250
The only ones left at Central right now are Father and Sloth.

166
00:11:39,510 --> 00:11:42,510
Greed! What the hell are you thinking?!

167
00:11:43,720 --> 00:11:45,010
Told you earlier, didn't I?

168
00:11:45,430 --> 00:11:47,720
I'm going to become the king of the world.

169
00:11:56,980 --> 00:12:01,610
Don't you think there's been a lot of Ishbalans in Central lately?

170
00:12:01,820 --> 00:12:03,150
Yeah, man.

171
00:12:03,150 --> 00:12:07,120
I heard there's a group of them near the abandoned building to the west.

172
00:12:07,120 --> 00:12:08,950
Speaking of Ishbalans...

173
00:12:08,950 --> 00:12:11,950
Remember the lad with the cross-shaped scar who used to live here?

174
00:12:11,950 --> 00:12:13,040
I wonder how he's doing.

175
00:12:15,460 --> 00:12:17,840
Yo, speak of the devil!

176
00:12:17,840 --> 00:12:20,250
We were just talking about you!

177
00:12:20,550 --> 00:12:23,510
I'm looking for a slum by the name of Kanama.

178
00:12:25,180 --> 00:12:29,350
Kanama is located on the edge of town,
in the forest to the south.

179
00:12:29,350 --> 00:12:31,350
I see. Thanks.

180
00:12:32,140 --> 00:12:34,600
Oh yeah, isn't the little girl with you?

181
00:12:35,810 --> 00:12:39,110
You know, the one who was
carrying around a black and white cat.

182
00:12:39,110 --> 00:12:42,110
She actually came back here a little while ago.

183
00:12:42,110 --> 00:12:42,990
What?!

184
00:12:42,990 --> 00:12:45,490
She didn't go back to her country?

185
00:12:45,490 --> 00:12:47,410
What is she up to?

186
00:12:49,070 --> 00:12:51,290
You guys finally did it!

187
00:12:52,200 --> 00:12:53,370
What are you talking about?

188
00:12:53,370 --> 00:12:55,040
You guys were the ones behind it, right?

189
00:12:55,040 --> 00:12:58,290
The ones who blew up Bradley in his train in the east.

190
00:12:58,290 --> 00:12:59,000
Blew up?!

191
00:12:59,210 --> 00:13:01,550
Huh? Was I wrong?

192
00:13:01,550 --> 00:13:02,800
This is news to us.

193
00:13:02,800 --> 00:13:08,760
Well, I figured you teamed up
with the other Ishbalans and did it.

194
00:13:08,760 --> 00:13:13,470
Well, everyone was saying that
they were going to commit terrorism.

195
00:13:13,470 --> 00:13:17,020
They didn't gather here to do such a thing.

196
00:13:17,690 --> 00:13:22,770
They're good friends of ours who seek to change this country in a method other than terrorism.

197
00:13:43,050 --> 00:13:46,630
I should stop being so enthusiastic about my work.

198
00:13:47,050 --> 00:13:51,010
Because of that, I've soiled my new suit.

199
00:13:52,220 --> 00:13:55,430
The real performance starts after daybreak.

200
00:14:04,530 --> 00:14:05,530
It's useless.

201
00:14:06,280 --> 00:14:10,280
There's no way my dad would make it so easy for a child to be able to break through.

202
00:14:16,290 --> 00:14:20,170
This is what happens when you make fun of humans so much.

203
00:14:20,710 --> 00:14:24,380
You guys don't know anything about us.

204
00:14:24,960 --> 00:14:27,970
You shouldn't think that everything will go your way.

205
00:14:29,420 --> 00:14:31,340
Same with that scheme.

206
00:14:31,340 --> 00:14:33,640
From my perspective, it's just careless planning.

207
00:14:34,760 --> 00:14:35,760
Careless?

208
00:14:36,220 --> 00:14:37,430
That's right.

209
00:14:37,430 --> 00:14:39,270
You call us human sacrifices,

210
00:14:39,270 --> 00:14:43,480
and it seems as though you're planning on using us to accomplish something...

211
00:14:43,480 --> 00:14:47,780
What if we were to escape outside the country for the fear of our own safety?

212
00:14:47,780 --> 00:14:51,150
At that point, your plan would have been completely ruined.

213
00:14:53,490 --> 00:14:59,250
As you say, there are humans who believe that their safety comes first.

214
00:15:00,120 --> 00:15:01,290
However...

215
00:15:01,870 --> 00:15:04,920
Yes, for example, Wrath's wife.

216
00:15:05,840 --> 00:15:10,470
There once was a time when I was about to be hit by a car in town.

217
00:15:10,880 --> 00:15:16,760
She tried to save me, ready to sacrifice her own life.

218
00:15:17,930 --> 00:15:21,440
Though she doesn't know I'm a homunculus,

219
00:15:21,980 --> 00:15:25,860
I was completely taken aback by her desperate action.

220
00:15:29,320 --> 00:15:34,620
I've always had a father, but never a mother.

221
00:15:34,620 --> 00:15:38,120
That's why, to be honest, her existence was fascinating.

222
00:15:38,660 --> 00:15:41,330
I began to wonder whether that's what having a mother was like.

223
00:15:42,500 --> 00:15:44,210
Wrath's wife...

224
00:15:44,670 --> 00:15:46,790
Madam Bradley, right?

225
00:15:47,380 --> 00:15:48,500
That's right.

226
00:15:51,130 --> 00:15:53,800
I can't believe how low you are to deceive such a kind soul...

227
00:15:54,130 --> 00:15:56,890
You're right. It was  as if we were playing a game of house.

228
00:15:59,850 --> 00:16:02,930
But it was fun living with her,

229
00:16:03,230 --> 00:16:04,480
and I do love her.

230
00:16:05,560 --> 00:16:06,310
Then-

231
00:16:06,310 --> 00:16:07,270
There are...

232
00:16:10,320 --> 00:16:17,910
There are humans, like Wrath's wife, who would throw away their own life to protect something dear to them.

233
00:16:19,160 --> 00:16:22,370
And those of you who were chosen to be human sacrifices,

234
00:16:22,370 --> 00:16:26,580
possess a strong heart, even out of those people.

235
00:16:27,130 --> 00:16:30,130
There's no way you'd throw away this country and flee.

236
00:16:30,630 --> 00:16:33,800
For instance, you came back here to fight.

237
00:16:36,260 --> 00:16:40,260
There's not a hint of carelessness in our plan.

238
00:16:52,610 --> 00:16:53,490
Colonel.

239
00:16:56,150 --> 00:16:57,700
It's almost time.

240
00:16:59,830 --> 00:17:00,660
Right.

241
00:17:08,830 --> 00:17:10,790
Let's go, Lieutenant.

242
00:17:25,270 --> 00:17:26,850
What in the name of...

243
00:17:27,390 --> 00:17:30,400
What happened here?

244
00:17:30,770 --> 00:17:33,480
And what is this mound?

245
00:17:34,900 --> 00:17:37,110
Well, if it isn't Jerso and Zampano!

246
00:17:38,110 --> 00:17:38,990
Darius!

247
00:17:40,870 --> 00:17:45,370
D-Don't tell me Kimblee sent you here to eliminate us?

248
00:17:45,370 --> 00:17:46,120
Huh?

249
00:17:46,120 --> 00:17:47,580
What are you, high?

250
00:17:47,580 --> 00:17:50,330
I stopped working for Kimblee months ago.

251
00:17:50,330 --> 00:17:53,670
You're just saying that to get us off guard, and then you're planning to kill us!

252
00:17:53,670 --> 00:17:54,760
I'm not!

253
00:17:54,920 --> 00:17:56,800
I can't trust you!

254
00:17:56,800 --> 00:18:00,510
Heinkel's probably hiding somewhere over there, ready to ambush us.

255
00:18:00,510 --> 00:18:01,850
Quit being so insistent, idiot!

256
00:18:00,550 --> 00:18:01,850
Doctor Marcoh!

257
00:18:01,850 --> 00:18:02,970
What did you just call me?!

258
00:18:02,970 --> 00:18:04,100
You want to fight, Porky Pig?!

259
00:18:02,970 --> 00:18:04,100
Edward.

260
00:18:04,100 --> 00:18:05,270
That's Zampano!

261
00:18:05,270 --> 00:18:05,970
You-

262
00:18:05,270 --> 00:18:06,980
So Scar was with you guys.

263
00:18:05,970 --> 00:18:06,980
What are you saying?!

264
00:18:06,980 --> 00:18:08,940
The gorilla said it!

265
00:18:08,190 --> 00:18:11,270
Sorry to rush you when you just arrived, but we should make arrangements asap-

266
00:18:13,230 --> 00:18:14,360
Hey!

267
00:18:14,360 --> 00:18:17,070
Why can't pigs, fatties and gorillas learn to get along?!

268
00:18:17,070 --> 00:18:18,820
Are you picking a fight, punk?!

269
00:18:21,620 --> 00:18:25,950
Oh, so you guys really did stop working for Kimblee.

270
00:18:26,580 --> 00:18:31,290
If we kept working for him, he'd just dispose of us.

271
00:18:31,290 --> 00:18:32,830
Definitely.

272
00:18:33,040 --> 00:18:36,510
Well thanks to that, we're fugitives now,

273
00:18:36,510 --> 00:18:38,050
but it does feel nice.

274
00:18:38,050 --> 00:18:39,220
Yeah.

275
00:18:39,880 --> 00:18:40,970
Also,

276
00:18:41,340 --> 00:18:44,680
those guys definitely won't abandon us.

277
00:18:50,310 --> 00:18:53,270
It'll finally begin once the sun comes up.

278
00:18:54,020 --> 00:18:55,190
Yeah.

279
00:18:55,570 --> 00:18:58,400
I hope we'll all live to see the next day.

280
00:19:00,240 --> 00:19:02,030
Looks like they've come to terms.

281
00:19:04,490 --> 00:19:06,410
Where did the old man run off to?

282
00:19:08,750 --> 00:19:10,290
He went to go scout out the town.

283
00:19:10,580 --> 00:19:11,830
Alone?

284
00:19:11,830 --> 00:19:12,790
Yeah.

285
00:19:13,210 --> 00:19:16,710
He said that it would end up being more convenient,

286
00:19:16,710 --> 00:19:19,420
since he's the only one whose face hasn't been seen by the enemy.

287
00:19:20,050 --> 00:19:24,470
He said he'd go and check up on a couple of things, such as Colonel Mustang's movements,

288
00:19:25,720 --> 00:19:28,970
but for the most part, I think he's worried about the whereabouts of Lin.

289
00:19:28,970 --> 00:19:31,140
Ah, makes sense.

290
00:19:31,520 --> 00:19:34,020
Are you done making arrangements with Scar and them?

291
00:19:34,520 --> 00:19:35,360
Yeah.

292
00:19:36,400 --> 00:19:38,400
The plan has been decided.

293
00:19:38,980 --> 00:19:40,190
I see.

294
00:19:40,190 --> 00:19:41,490
So it's time at last.

295
00:19:49,160 --> 00:19:52,080
Your brother is pretty gutsy.

296
00:19:52,080 --> 00:19:55,130
He's trapped in there with that monster in pitch darkness, after all.

297
00:19:55,920 --> 00:19:58,590
If it were me, I would have gone crazy by now.

298
00:19:58,590 --> 00:19:59,500
Yeah.

299
00:20:00,920 --> 00:20:03,470
Al's giving it his all.

300
00:20:04,720 --> 00:20:05,760
Now, the rest...

301
00:20:06,550 --> 00:20:08,310
...is up to us!

302
00:20:26,530 --> 00:20:28,200
The Promised Day...

303
00:20:28,740 --> 00:20:29,950
...is here!

304
00:20:44,470 --> 00:20:49,430
The promise we never made

305
00:20:44,470 --> 00:20:49,430
Kawashita hazu no nai yakasoku ga

306
00:20:49,430 --> 00:20:50,220
yet again

307
00:20:49,430 --> 00:20:50,220
Kyou mo

308
00:20:50,220 --> 00:20:55,060
tries to snatch our future away from us.

309
00:20:50,220 --> 00:20:55,060
Bokura no mirai wo ubaou to suru

310
00:20:56,690 --> 00:21:00,650
Why is it that we can't rejoice

311
00:20:56,690 --> 00:21:00,650
Hoshigatteita mono wo te ni shitemo

312
00:21:00,650 --> 00:21:01,650
straight from the heart

313
00:21:00,650 --> 00:21:01,650
Sunao ni

314
00:21:01,650 --> 00:21:06,610
when we obtain something we've always been after?

315
00:21:01,650 --> 00:21:06,610
Umaku waraenai nowa nazedarou

316
00:21:07,280 --> 00:21:12,330
The overflowing tears aren't from feebleness or remorse.

317
00:21:07,280 --> 00:21:12,330
Afureru namida wo yowasa ya koukai ja nai

318
00:21:12,990 --> 00:21:17,120
They're fragments born from agony.

319
00:21:12,990 --> 00:21:17,120
Itami ga unda kakera de

320
00:21:18,790 --> 00:21:22,170
Of all the moments and destinies,

321
00:21:18,790 --> 00:21:22,170
Donna shunkan datte unmei datte

322
00:21:22,170 --> 00:21:30,930
I realized there's one absolute certainty.

323
00:21:22,170 --> 00:21:30,930
Hitotsu dake tashika na mono ga aru to shitta

324
00:21:30,930 --> 00:21:33,470
Even if things get tough and I'm at my limit

325
00:21:30,930 --> 00:21:33,470
Genkai datte konnan datte

326
00:21:33,470 --> 00:21:37,480
I refuse to give up.

327
00:21:33,470 --> 00:21:37,480
Akirametakunaiyo

328
00:21:37,480 --> 00:21:42,360
Please, don't let go.

329
00:21:37,480 --> 00:21:42,360
Konomama hanasanaide

330
00:21:42,360 --> 00:21:50,200
I can feel the warmth of your right hand

331
00:21:42,360 --> 00:21:50,200
Kataku nigirishimeta kimi no migite no nukumori

332
00:21:50,200 --> 00:21:53,870
where it's tightly joined with my left.

333
00:21:50,200 --> 00:21:53,870
Koko ni arukara

334
00:22:02,710 --> 00:22:05,090
Denny! Denny!

335
00:22:05,090 --> 00:22:07,590
Hey, Denny!

336
00:22:07,590 --> 00:22:08,970
Shut up...

337
00:22:09,970 --> 00:22:11,390
What do you want?

338
00:22:11,390 --> 00:22:12,680
You need to wake up!

339
00:22:12,680 --> 00:22:14,600
Or else it'll begin!

340
00:22:14,600 --> 00:22:17,270
What'll begin?

341
00:22:17,270 --> 00:22:18,560
The solar eclipse!

342
00:22:18,560 --> 00:22:20,020
Solar eclipse?

343
00:22:20,810 --> 00:22:24,610
Geez... what time do you think it is?

344
00:22:24,940 --> 00:22:27,690
It's way too early for the solar eclipse to begin.

345
00:22:28,110 --> 00:22:29,740
H-Hey! Don't look at the sun with that!

346
00:22:29,740 --> 00:22:31,030
You'll go blind!

347
00:22:31,240 --> 00:22:33,370
I know that.

348
00:22:35,450 --> 00:22:36,910
Come here, Brother!

349
00:22:36,910 --> 00:22:38,500
There's smoke rising from town!

350
00:22:47,420 --> 00:22:49,760
Don't leave the house today, got it?!

351
00:22:56,430 --> 00:23:00,230
Cedi Squad in the western district reporting.
We've discovered Mustang and his men in District C75.

352
00:23:00,230 --> 00:23:01,600
We're currently engaging.

353
00:23:01,600 --> 00:23:05,480
However, they have the Führer President's wife as hostage,

354
00:23:05,480 --> 00:23:07,730
and it's very difficult for us to attack...

355
00:23:07,730 --> 00:23:09,740
I don't care. Attack.

356
00:23:09,740 --> 00:23:10,610
Huh?

357
00:23:13,780 --> 00:23:16,580
As long as Roy Mustang stays alive, it's fine.

358
00:23:16,580 --> 00:23:18,500
The woman means nothing to us.

359
00:23:19,200 --> 00:23:22,330
Have her killed along with Mustang's men.

360
00:23:28,130 --> 00:23:29,010
Freeze!

361
00:23:37,760 --> 00:23:39,140
Will you shoot?

362
00:23:43,730 --> 00:23:47,150
Shoot everyone except for Colonel Mustang!

363
00:23:59,080 --> 00:24:04,290
The peace-accustomed masses are oblivious to the crisis right before their eyes.

364
00:24:05,130 --> 00:24:08,800
They can't even begin to imagine the destruction awaiting them.

365
00:24:10,090 --> 00:24:14,380
Next time, Fullmetal Alchemist:

366
00:24:14,380 --> 00:24:18,410
Episode 50, Upheaval in Central.

367
00:24:14,400 --> 00:24:18,410
Upheavel in Central

368
00:24:18,930 --> 00:24:23,520
The weak reel in loss, and the strong trample them down.

369
00:24:23,520 --> 00:24:26,020
That is war.
